<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine farmers had harvested 75.2 percent of their drought-hit 1996/97 soybean crop by May 9, compared to only 42.0 percent progress by the same date last year, the Agriculture Secretariat said in weekly crop report Thursday.</p>
<p>Maize harvesting reached 77.1 percent, compared to 67.9 percent by the same date last year. Peanut harvesting was 51.4 percent complete with projected final output of 300,000 tonnes. Rice harvesting was 97.7 percent complete, with total season production seen at 1.1 million tonnes. Sorghum production was seen totaling 2.56 million tonnes.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..................Yield</p>
<p> Wheat     6,983  100.0(100.0) 6,694.4  100.0   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Maize     3,901  100.0(100.0) 2,549.0   77.1  (67.9)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Soybeans  6,591  100.0(100.0) 4,833.1   75.2  (42.0)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sunflower 3,088  100.0(100.0) 2,960.3   99.5  (99.8)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sorghum     784  100.0(100.0)   501.6   69.8  (54.9)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Cotton	952  100.0  (n/a)   475.9   53.9  (40.2)    (n/a)</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
